for the report. Could you make a self-contained reproducible test case that does not depend on python and 3rd party repository? Also could you explain what are the circumstances of this problem? If I read your report correctly, then it is that your 3rd party application uses bdwgc alongside ECL by calling directly libgc functions, and when you push a lot of roots, then it breaks. Is that correct? Or can ECL end in this state on its own?\n\nAlso please note, that we have an issue template with structured way to report the host system:\nhttps://gitlab.com/embeddable-common-lisp/ecl/-/blob/develop/CONTRIBUTING\n\nIf you could specify: observed behavior (with log) and expected behavior too.\n\nPS as noted in the linked file, we expect that all communication and patches are not mediated by an LLM.","note_html":"\u003cp data-sourcepos=\"1:1-1:457\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eHello. Thank you for the report. Could you make a self-contained reproducible test case that does not depend on python and 3rd party repository? Also could you explain what are the circumstances of this problem? If I read your report correctly, then it is that your 3rd party application uses bdwgc alongside ECL by calling directly libgc functions, and when you push a lot of roots, then it breaks. Is that correct? Or can ECL end in this state on its own?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp data-sourcepos=\"3:1-4:73\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eAlso please note, that we have an issue template with structured way to report the host system:\n\u003ca data-sourcepos=\"4:1-4:73\" href=\"https://gitlab.com/embeddable-common-lisp/ecl/-/blob/develop/CONTRIBUTING\"\u003ehttps://gitlab.com/embeddable-common-lisp/ecl/-/blob/develop/CONTRIBUTING\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp data-sourcepos=\"6:1-6:77\" dir=\"auto\"\u003eIf you could specify: observed behavior (with log) and expected behavior too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp data-sourcepos=\"8:1-8:104\" dir=\"auto\"\u003ePS as noted in the linked file, we expect that all communication and patches are not mediated by an LLM.\u003c/p\u003e","body_first_line_html":"\u003cp\u003eHello. Thank you for the report. Could you make a self-contained reproducible test case that does not depend on python and...\u003c/p\u003e","last_edited_at":"2026-10-24T13:21:44.897Z","last_edited_by":{"id":105521,"username":"jackdaniel","public_email":"daniel@turtleware.eu","name":"Daniel Kochmański","state":"active","locked":false,"avatar_url":"https://gitlab.com/uploads/-/system/user/avatar/105521/glider.jpg?v=1792847269","show_status":false,"path":"/jackdaniel","bot":false,"user_type":"human"},"current_user":{"can_edit":false,"can_award_emoji":false,"can_resolve":false,"can_resolve_discussion":false},"suggestions":[],"resolved":false,"resolved_by":null,"resolved_by_push":false,"is_noteable_author":false,"discussion_id":"ada0f26d923edb284b4868c7fda5aee8de720443","emoji_awardable":true,"award_emoji":[],"report_abuse_path":"/-/abuse_reports/add_category","noteable_note_url":"https://gitlab.com/embeddable-common-lisp/ecl/-/work_items/860#note_4082425916","cached_markdown_version":2228233,"duo_session_id_triggered":null,"duo_session_agent_name":null,"duo_session_status":null,"duo_session_url":null,"human_access":"Owner","is_contributor":false,"project_name":"ECL","toggle_award_path":"/embeddable-common-lisp/ecl/notes/4082425916/toggle_award_emoji","path":"/embeddable-common-lisp/ecl/notes/4082425916"}]}]